{
 "1": "<figure class=\"fig\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 336\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"The same twelve customers plotted twice. Left: each point carries a label, bought or did not buy, and a learned boundary separates them. Right: the points have no labels and the algorithm finds two clusters.\">\n<text x=\"190\" y=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:14px;font-weight:600\">Supervised: every point has a label</text>\n<text x=\"550\" y=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:14px;font-weight:600\">Unsupervised: no labels</text>\n<circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"44\" r=\"6\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\"/><text x=\"92\" y=\"49\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:13px\">Bought</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"38\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" style=\"fill:var(--panel);stroke:var(--live);stroke-width:2\"/><text x=\"180\" y=\"49\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:13px\">Did not buy</text>\n<text x=\"550\" y=\"49\" text-anchor=\"middle\" style=\"font-size:13px;fill:var(--muted)\">the algorithm groups points by distance</text>\n<g style=\"stroke:var(--line2);stroke-width:1.5\">\n<line x1=\"50\" y1=\"270\" x2=\"335\" y2=\"270\"/><line x1=\"50\" y1=\"270\" x2=\"50\" y2=\"60\"/>\n<line x1=\"410\" y1=\"270\" x2=\"695\" y2=\"270\"/><line x1=\"410\" y1=\"270\" x2=\"410\" y2=\"60\"/>\n</g>\n<text x=\"190\" y=\"292\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:13px\">Monthly visits</text>\n<text x=\"550\" y=\"292\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:13px\">Monthly visits</text>\n<text x=\"34\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 34 165)\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:13px\">Spend (₹ thousand)</text>\n<text x=\"394\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 394 165)\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:13px\">Spend (₹ thousand)</text>\n<line x1=\"120\" y1=\"123\" x2=\"246\" y2=\"217.5\" style=\"stroke:var(--next);stroke-width:2;stroke-dasharray:7 5\"/>\n<text x=\"232\" y=\"240\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:13px;fill:var(--next)\">learned boundary</text>\n<g style=\"fill:var(--panel);stroke:var(--live);stroke-width:2\">\n<rect x=\"86\" y=\"222\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\"/><rect x=\"100\" y=\"197\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\"/><rect x=\"122\" y=\"226\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\"/><rect x=\"134\" y=\"203\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\"/><rect x=\"78\" y=\"188\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\"/><rect x=\"114\" y=\"172\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\"/>\n</g>\n<g style=\"fill:var(--accent)\">\n<circle cx=\"218\" cy=\"133\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"246\" cy=\"148\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"260\" cy=\"110\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"229\" cy=\"100\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"282\" cy=\"131\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"207\" cy=\"115\" r=\"6\"/>\n</g>\n<circle cx=\"204\" cy=\"168\" r=\"7\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2;stroke-dasharray:3 2\"/>\n<text x=\"216\" y=\"182\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:13px\">new → Bought</text>\n<ellipse cx=\"472\" cy=\"205\" rx=\"52\" ry=\"44\" style=\"fill:var(--accent-soft);stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:1.5;stroke-dasharray:6 4\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"603\" cy=\"123\" rx=\"60\" ry=\"42\" style=\"fill:var(--next-soft);stroke:var(--next);stroke-width:1.5;stroke-dasharray:6 4\"/>\n<g style=\"fill:var(--muted)\">\n<circle cx=\"452\" cy=\"228\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"466\" cy=\"203\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"488\" cy=\"232\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"500\" cy=\"209\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"444\" cy=\"194\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"480\" cy=\"178\" r=\"6\"/>\n<circle cx=\"578\" cy=\"133\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"606\" cy=\"148\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"620\" cy=\"110\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"589\" cy=\"100\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"642\" cy=\"131\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"567\" cy=\"115\" r=\"6\"/>\n</g>\n<text x=\"530\" y=\"222\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:600\">Cluster 1</text>\n<text x=\"603\" y=\"74\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:600\">Cluster 2</text>\n<text x=\"190\" y=\"318\" text-anchor=\"middle\" style=\"font-size:13px;fill:var(--muted)\">Output: a rule that predicts a label</text>\n<text x=\"550\" y=\"318\" text-anchor=\"middle\" style=\"font-size:13px;fill:var(--muted)\">Output: groups and their centres</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>Figure 5.1.1</b> The same twelve shop customers seen two ways. On the left each point carries its label, so a supervised learner can draw a boundary and predict the label of a new customer. On the right the labels are missing, so an unsupervised learner can only group points that sit close together. Here the clusters match the labels; in real data they often do not.</figcaption>\n</figure>",
 "2": "<figure class=\"fig\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 362\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Scatter plot of marks against weekly study hours for five students, with the least-squares line y-hat equals 42.8 plus 3.7 x and the vertical residual of each point\">\n<path d=\"M80 300 H668 M80 300 V36 M176 300 v5 M272 300 v5 M368 300 v5 M464 300 v5 M560 300 v5 M656 300 v5 M80 248 h-5 M80 196 h-5 M80 144 h-5 M80 92 h-5 M80 40 h-5\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:var(--line2);stroke-width:1.5\"/>\n<g fill=\"currentColor\" text-anchor=\"middle\" style=\"font-size:13px\">\n<text x=\"80\" y=\"320\">0</text><text x=\"176\" y=\"320\">2</text><text x=\"272\" y=\"320\">4</text><text x=\"368\" y=\"320\">6</text><text x=\"464\" y=\"320\">8</text><text x=\"560\" y=\"320\">10</text><text x=\"656\" y=\"320\">12</text>\n</g>\n<g fill=\"currentColor\" text-anchor=\"end\" style=\"font-size:13px\">\n<text x=\"70\" y=\"304\">40</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"252\">50</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"200\">60</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"148\">70</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"96\">80</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"44\">90</text>\n</g>\n<text x=\"374\" y=\"348\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:13px\">Hours of study per week (x)</text>\n<text x=\"26\" y=\"170\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 26 170)\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:13px\">Marks out of 100 (y)</text>\n<line x1=\"80\" y1=\"285.4\" x2=\"656\" y2=\"54.6\" style=\"stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:2.5\"/>\n<g style=\"stroke:var(--live);stroke-width:2.5\">\n<line x1=\"176\" y1=\"248\" x2=\"176\" y2=\"247\"/><line x1=\"272\" y1=\"206.4\" x2=\"272\" y2=\"208.5\"/><line x1=\"368\" y1=\"164.8\" x2=\"368\" y2=\"170\"/><line x1=\"464\" y1=\"144\" x2=\"464\" y2=\"131.5\"/><line x1=\"560\" y1=\"86.8\" x2=\"560\" y2=\"93\"/>\n</g>\n<g style=\"fill:var(--panel);stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2\">\n<circle cx=\"176\" cy=\"248\" r=\"5.5\"/><circle cx=\"272\" cy=\"206.4\" r=\"5.5\"/><circle cx=\"368\" cy=\"164.8\" r=\"5.5\"/><circle cx=\"464\" cy=\"144\" r=\"5.5\"/><circle cx=\"560\" cy=\"86.8\" r=\"5.5\"/>\n</g>\n<g style=\"font-size:13px;fill:var(--live);font-weight:600\">\n<text x=\"186\" y=\"268\">e = −0.2</text><text x=\"282\" y=\"228\">e = +0.4</text><text x=\"356\" y=\"156\" text-anchor=\"end\">e = +1.0</text><text x=\"476\" y=\"160\">e = −2.4</text><text x=\"572\" y=\"104\">e = +1.2</text>\n</g>\n<rect x=\"364\" y=\"166\" width=\"8\" height=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--next)\"/>\n<text x=\"384\" y=\"200\" style=\"font-size:13px;fill:var(--next)\">line passes through (x̄, ȳ) = (6, 65)</text>\n<text x=\"420\" y=\"56\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:14px;font-weight:600\">ŷ = 42.8 + 3.7x,  R² = 0.985</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>Figure 5.2.1</b> The least-squares line for the five students of the worked example. Each orange segment is a residual e = y − ŷ, the vertical miss that least squares squares and adds up (SSE = 8.4). The residuals add to zero and the line passes through the mean point (6, 65).</figcaption>\n</figure>",
 "3": "<figure class=\"fig\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 350\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Sigmoid curve of pass probability against hours of revision for z equals minus 4 plus 0.8 x, with failed students along the bottom, passed students along the top, the 0.5 threshold and the decision boundary at 5 hours\">\n<path d=\"M80 290 H650 M80 290 V40 M192 290 v5 M304 290 v5 M416 290 v5 M528 290 v5 M640 290 v5 M80 170 h-5 M80 50 h-5\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:var(--line2);stroke-width:1.5\"/>\n<g fill=\"currentColor\" text-anchor=\"middle\" style=\"font-size:13px\">\n<text x=\"80\" y=\"310\">0</text><text x=\"192\" y=\"310\">2</text><text x=\"304\" y=\"310\">4</text><text x=\"416\" y=\"310\">6</text><text x=\"528\" y=\"310\">8</text><text x=\"640\" y=\"310\">10</text>\n</g>\n<g fill=\"currentColor\" text-anchor=\"end\" style=\"font-size:13px\"><text x=\"70\" y=\"294\">0</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"174\">0.5</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"54\">1</text></g>\n<text x=\"365\" y=\"336\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:13px\">Hours of revision (x)</text>\n<text x=\"28\" y=\"170\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 28 170)\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:13px\">P(pass) = σ(z)</text>\n<line x1=\"80\" y1=\"170\" x2=\"650\" y2=\"170\" style=\"stroke:var(--line2);stroke-width:1.5;stroke-dasharray:6 4\"/>\n<text x=\"645\" y=\"188\" text-anchor=\"end\" style=\"font-size:13px;fill:var(--muted)\">threshold p = 0.5</text>\n<line x1=\"360\" y1=\"290\" x2=\"360\" y2=\"56\" style=\"stroke:var(--next);stroke-width:1.5;stroke-dasharray:6 4\"/>\n<text x=\"368\" y=\"40\" style=\"font-size:13px;fill:var(--next)\">decision boundary: x = 5 hours (z = 0)</text>\n<path d=\"M80.0 285.7 L94.0 284.7 L108.0 283.6 L122.0 282.2 L136.0 280.6 L150.0 278.6 L164.0 276.2 L178.0 273.4 L192.0 270.0 L206.0 266.1 L220.0 261.4 L234.0 256.0 L248.0 249.7 L262.0 242.5 L276.0 234.4 L290.0 225.5 L304.0 215.6 L318.0 205.0 L332.0 193.7 L346.0 182.0 L360.0 170.0 L374.0 158.0 L388.0 146.3 L402.0 135.0 L416.0 124.4 L430.0 114.5 L444.0 105.6 L458.0 97.5 L472.0 90.3 L486.0 84.0 L500.0 78.6 L514.0 73.9 L528.0 70.0 L542.0 66.6 L556.0 63.8 L570.0 61.4 L584.0 59.4 L598.0 57.8 L612.0 56.4 L626.0 55.3 L640.0 54.3\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:2.5\"/>\n<g style=\"fill:var(--panel);stroke:var(--live);stroke-width:2\">\n<rect x=\"131\" y=\"285\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\"/><rect x=\"187\" y=\"285\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\"/><rect x=\"215\" y=\"285\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\"/><rect x=\"271\" y=\"285\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\"/><rect x=\"299\" y=\"285\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\"/><rect x=\"411\" y=\"285\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\"/>\n</g>\n<g style=\"fill:var(--accent)\">\n<circle cx=\"332\" cy=\"50\" r=\"5\"/><circle cx=\"388\" cy=\"50\" r=\"5\"/><circle cx=\"444\" cy=\"50\" r=\"5\"/><circle cx=\"472\" cy=\"50\" r=\"5\"/><circle cx=\"528\" cy=\"50\" r=\"5\"/><circle cx=\"584\" cy=\"50\" r=\"5\"/>\n</g>\n<circle cx=\"101\" cy=\"58\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\"/><text x=\"112\" y=\"62\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:13px\">passed (y = 1)</text>\n<rect x=\"440\" y=\"271\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" style=\"fill:var(--panel);stroke:var(--live);stroke-width:2\"/><text x=\"456\" y=\"281\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:13px\">failed (y = 0)</text>\n<g style=\"fill:var(--live)\"><circle cx=\"248\" cy=\"249.7\" r=\"5\"/><circle cx=\"360\" cy=\"170\" r=\"5\"/><circle cx=\"472\" cy=\"90.3\" r=\"5\"/></g>\n<g style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:600\" fill=\"currentColor\">\n<text x=\"258\" y=\"268\">p(3) = 0.17</text><text x=\"372\" y=\"190\">p(5) = 0.50</text><text x=\"484\" y=\"110\">p(7) = 0.83</text>\n</g>\n<text x=\"96\" y=\"110\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:14px;font-weight:600\">z = −4 + 0.8x</text>\n<text x=\"96\" y=\"132\" style=\"font-size:13px;fill:var(--muted)\">odds × 2.23 per extra hour</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>Figure 5.3.1</b> The fitted curve of the worked example, p = σ(−4 + 0.8x). Students who failed sit at p = 0, those who passed at p = 1. The curve crosses the 0.5 threshold where z = 0, at x = 5 hours, which is the decision boundary. Notice that one extra hour changes p most near the middle of the S and hardly at all at the ends.</figcaption>\n</figure>",
 "4": "<figure class=\"fig\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 330\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"The decision tree learned from ten evenings: Weather at the root; Cloudy gives Play, Rainy gives No play, and Sunny leads to a test on Exam next day, where No gives Play and Yes gives No play\">\n<g style=\"stroke:var(--line2);stroke-width:2\">\n<line x1=\"360\" y1=\"78\" x2=\"160\" y2=\"142\"/><line x1=\"360\" y1=\"78\" x2=\"380\" y2=\"146\"/><line x1=\"360\" y1=\"78\" x2=\"590\" y2=\"146\"/>\n<line x1=\"160\" y1=\"190\" x2=\"90\" y2=\"258\"/><line x1=\"160\" y1=\"190\" x2=\"240\" y2=\"258\"/>\n</g>\n<rect x=\"250\" y=\"22\" width=\"220\" height=\"56\" rx=\"10\" style=\"fill:var(--accent-soft);stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:2\"/>\n<text x=\"360\" y=\"45\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:15px;font-weight:700\">Weather?</text>\n<text x=\"360\" y=\"66\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:13px\">10 rows: 5 Yes, 5 No · H = 1</text>\n<rect x=\"60\" y=\"142\" width=\"200\" height=\"48\" rx=\"10\" style=\"fill:var(--accent-soft);stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:2\"/>\n<text x=\"160\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:14px;font-weight:700\">Exam next day?</text>\n<text x=\"160\" y=\"181\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:13px\">4 rows: 2 Yes, 2 No</text>\n<g style=\"fill:var(--next-soft);stroke:var(--next);stroke-width:2\">\n<rect x=\"320\" y=\"146\" width=\"120\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\"/><rect x=\"30\" y=\"258\" width=\"120\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\"/>\n</g>\n<g style=\"fill:var(--live-soft);stroke:var(--live);stroke-width:2\">\n<rect x=\"530\" y=\"146\" width=\"120\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\"/><rect x=\"180\" y=\"258\" width=\"120\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\"/>\n</g>\n<g text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:13px\">\n<text x=\"380\" y=\"165\" style=\"font-weight:700\">Play</text><text x=\"380\" y=\"182\">3 Yes, 0 No</text>\n<text x=\"590\" y=\"165\" style=\"font-weight:700\">No play</text><text x=\"590\" y=\"182\">0 Yes, 3 No</text>\n<text x=\"90\" y=\"277\" style=\"font-weight:700\">Play</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"294\">2 Yes, 0 No</text>\n<text x=\"240\" y=\"277\" style=\"font-weight:700\">No play</text><text x=\"240\" y=\"294\">0 Yes, 2 No</text>\n</g>\n<g style=\"font-size:13px;fill:var(--accent);font-weight:600\">\n<text x=\"236\" y=\"104\" text-anchor=\"end\">Sunny</text><text x=\"384\" y=\"118\">Cloudy</text><text x=\"488\" y=\"104\">Rainy</text>\n<text x=\"112\" y=\"230\" text-anchor=\"end\">No</text><text x=\"212\" y=\"230\">Yes</text>\n</g>\n<rect x=\"340\" y=\"222\" width=\"370\" height=\"96\" rx=\"10\" style=\"fill:var(--panel);stroke:var(--line2);stroke-width:1.5\"/>\n<g fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:13px\">\n<text x=\"354\" y=\"242\" style=\"font-weight:700\">Information gain at the root</text>\n<text x=\"354\" y=\"260\">Weather 0.600 (chosen) · Exam 0.125 · Ground 0.000</text>\n<text x=\"354\" y=\"284\" style=\"font-weight:700\">Inside the Sunny branch (4 rows)</text>\n<text x=\"354\" y=\"302\">Exam 1.000 (chosen) · Ground 0.311</text>\n</g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>Figure 5.4.1</b> The ID3 tree for the cricket data. Blue boxes are tests, green leaves predict Play and orange leaves predict No play; each box shows how many training rows reach it. The panel lists the gains that decided each test. Notice that Ground never appears: it carried no information once Weather and Exam were known.</figcaption>\n</figure>",
 "5": "<figure class=\"fig\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 344\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A 2-2-1 network with inputs 0.5 and 1.0, weights 0.4, 0.3, minus 0.2 and 0.6 into two sigmoid hidden neurons with outputs 0.622, and weights 0.7 and minus 0.5 into a sigmoid output of 0.531 against a target of 1; error signals are shown in orange\">\n<defs><marker id=\"f55a\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" style=\"fill:var(--line2)\"/></marker></defs>\n<g text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:14px;font-weight:600\">\n<text x=\"110\" y=\"24\">Input layer</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"24\">Hidden layer (sigmoid)</text><text x=\"600\" y=\"24\">Output (sigmoid)</text>\n</g>\n<g style=\"stroke:var(--line2);stroke-width:2;fill:none\">\n<line x1=\"144\" y1=\"110\" x2=\"322\" y2=\"110\" marker-end=\"url(#f55a)\"/><line x1=\"144\" y1=\"250\" x2=\"322\" y2=\"250\" marker-end=\"url(#f55a)\"/>\n<line x1=\"139\" y1=\"127\" x2=\"327\" y2=\"233\" marker-end=\"url(#f55a)\"/><line x1=\"139\" y1=\"233\" x2=\"327\" y2=\"127\" marker-end=\"url(#f55a)\"/>\n<line x1=\"393\" y1=\"120\" x2=\"563\" y2=\"170\" marker-end=\"url(#f55a)\"/><line x1=\"393\" y1=\"240\" x2=\"563\" y2=\"190\" marker-end=\"url(#f55a)\"/>\n</g>\n<g style=\"fill:var(--panel);stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:2\">\n<circle cx=\"110\" cy=\"110\" r=\"34\"/><circle cx=\"110\" cy=\"250\" r=\"34\"/><circle cx=\"360\" cy=\"110\" r=\"34\"/><circle cx=\"360\" cy=\"250\" r=\"34\"/>\n</g>\n<circle cx=\"600\" cy=\"180\" r=\"34\" style=\"fill:var(--accent-soft);stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:2\"/>\n<g text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:13px\">\n<text x=\"110\" y=\"106\" style=\"font-weight:700\">x₁</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"123\">0.5</text>\n<text x=\"110\" y=\"246\" style=\"font-weight:700\">x₂</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"263\">1.0</text>\n<text x=\"360\" y=\"106\" style=\"font-weight:700\">h₁</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"123\">0.622</text>\n<text x=\"360\" y=\"246\" style=\"font-weight:700\">h₂</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"263\">0.622</text>\n<text x=\"600\" y=\"176\" style=\"font-weight:700\">o</text><text x=\"600\" y=\"193\">0.531</text>\n</g>\n<g style=\"font-size:13px;fill:var(--accent);font-weight:600\">\n<text x=\"233\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\">w₁₁ = 0.4</text><text x=\"233\" y=\"270\" text-anchor=\"middle\">w₂₂ = 0.6</text>\n<text x=\"196\" y=\"148\">w₁₂ = −0.2</text><text x=\"196\" y=\"226\">w₂₁ = 0.3</text>\n<text x=\"470\" y=\"126\" text-anchor=\"middle\">v₁ = 0.7</text><text x=\"470\" y=\"248\" text-anchor=\"middle\">v₂ = −0.5</text>\n</g>\n<g text-anchor=\"middle\" style=\"font-size:13px;fill:var(--live);font-weight:600\">\n<text x=\"360\" y=\"64\">δ₁ = −0.0192</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"304\">δ₂ = +0.0137</text><text x=\"600\" y=\"134\">δₒ = −0.1168</text>\n</g>\n<text x=\"600\" y=\"234\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:13px\">target t = 1</text>\n<text x=\"600\" y=\"252\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:13px\">E = ½(t − o)² = 0.110</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"332\" text-anchor=\"middle\" style=\"font-size:13px;fill:var(--accent)\">forward pass: values, left to right</text>\n<text x=\"530\" y=\"332\" text-anchor=\"middle\" style=\"font-size:13px;fill:var(--live)\">backward pass: δ's, right to left</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>Figure 5.5.1</b> The 2-2-1 network of the worked example. Black numbers inside the nodes come from the forward pass; orange δ values come from the backward pass and say how much each neuron's net input should change. Notice that δ₂ is positive although δₒ is negative, because h₂ reaches the output through the negative weight v₂.</figcaption>\n</figure>",
 "6": "<figure class=\"fig\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 330\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Two k-means iterations on six customers. Left: starting centroids at A and B give clusters A, C and B, D, E, F, and centroid 2 moves to 4.5, 4. Right: B switches to cluster 1 and the final centroids are 1.33, 1.33 and 5.33, 5\">\n<defs><marker id=\"f56a\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" style=\"fill:var(--live)\"/></marker></defs>\n<text x=\"176\" y=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:14px;font-weight:600\">Iteration 1: start at A and B</text>\n<text x=\"536\" y=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:14px;font-weight:600\">Iteration 2: B switches; final</text>\n<path d=\"M50 300 H310 M50 300 V40 M410 300 H670 M410 300 V40\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:var(--line2);stroke-width:1.5\"/>\n<text x=\"180\" y=\"320\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:13px\">visits per month</text>\n<text x=\"540\" y=\"320\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:13px\">visits per month</text>\n<text x=\"34\" y=\"170\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 34 170)\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:13px\">spend (₹ hundred)</text>\n<text x=\"394\" y=\"170\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 394 170)\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:13px\">spend (₹ hundred)</text>\n<g style=\"fill:var(--accent)\"><circle cx=\"86\" cy=\"264\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"86\" cy=\"228\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"446\" cy=\"264\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"482\" cy=\"264\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"446\" cy=\"228\" r=\"6\"/></g>\n<g style=\"fill:var(--live)\"><circle cx=\"122\" cy=\"264\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"230\" cy=\"156\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"266\" cy=\"120\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"230\" cy=\"84\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"590\" cy=\"156\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"626\" cy=\"120\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"590\" cy=\"84\" r=\"6\"/></g>\n<g fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:13px\">\n<text x=\"58\" y=\"293\">A(1,1)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"290\">B(2,1)</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"216\">C(1,2)</text><text x=\"242\" y=\"170\">D(5,4)</text><text x=\"276\" y=\"114\">E(6,5)</text><text x=\"242\" y=\"80\">F(5,6)</text>\n<text x=\"436\" y=\"284\">A</text><text x=\"482\" y=\"290\">B</text><text x=\"430\" y=\"224\">C</text><text x=\"600\" y=\"172\">D</text><text x=\"636\" y=\"116\">E</text><text x=\"600\" y=\"80\">F</text>\n</g>\n<g style=\"fill:none;stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.5;stroke-dasharray:3 2\"><circle cx=\"86\" cy=\"264\" r=\"11\"/><circle cx=\"122\" cy=\"264\" r=\"11\"/></g>\n<line x1=\"130\" y1=\"254\" x2=\"206\" y2=\"162\" style=\"stroke:var(--live);stroke-width:1.5;stroke-dasharray:5 3\" marker-end=\"url(#f56a)\"/>\n<g style=\"stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:3\"><path d=\"M80 246 h12 M86 240 v12 M206 156 h12 M212 150 v12 M452 252 h12 M458 246 v12 M596 120 h12 M602 114 v12\"/></g>\n<path d=\"M60 62 h12 M66 56 v12 M60 84 h12 M66 78 v12 M420 62 h12 M426 56 v12 M420 84 h12 M426 78 v12\" style=\"stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:3\"/>\n<g style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:600\" fill=\"currentColor\">\n<text x=\"80\" y=\"66\">c₁ moves to (1, 1.5)</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"88\">c₂ moves to (4.5, 4)</text>\n<text x=\"440\" y=\"66\">final c₁ = (1.33, 1.33)</text><text x=\"440\" y=\"88\">final c₂ = (5.33, 5)</text>\n</g>\n<text x=\"300\" y=\"290\" text-anchor=\"end\" style=\"font-size:13px;fill:var(--muted)\">WCSS = 23.5</text>\n<text x=\"660\" y=\"290\" text-anchor=\"end\" style=\"font-size:13px;fill:var(--muted)\">WCSS = 4.0</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>Figure 5.6.1</b> k-means with k = 2 on six customers (blue = cluster 1, orange = cluster 2; crosses are centroids). Starting both centroids at the close points A and B (dashed rings) puts B with the far group, and centroid c₂ jumps to (4.5, 4). In iteration 2, B is nearer c₁ and switches; nothing changes after that. WCSS falls from 23.5 to 4.0.</figcaption>\n</figure>",
 "7": "<figure class=\"fig\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 384\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Five students' maths and physics scores with the two principal component axes drawn through the mean point 4, 3; PC1 along the diagonal holds 90 percent of the variance; a bar chart shows eigenvalues 4.5 and 0.5\">\n<defs><marker id=\"f57a\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\"/></marker><marker id=\"f57b\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" style=\"fill:var(--live)\"/></marker></defs>\n<path d=\"M70 330 H480 M70 330 V24 M170 330 v5 M270 330 v5 M370 330 v5 M470 330 v5 M70 230 h-5 M70 130 h-5 M70 30 h-5\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:var(--line2);stroke-width:1.5\"/>\n<g fill=\"currentColor\" text-anchor=\"middle\" style=\"font-size:13px\"><text x=\"70\" y=\"350\">0</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"350\">2</text><text x=\"270\" y=\"350\">4</text><text x=\"370\" y=\"350\">6</text><text x=\"470\" y=\"350\">8</text></g>\n<g fill=\"currentColor\" text-anchor=\"end\" style=\"font-size:13px\"><text x=\"60\" y=\"334\">0</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"234\">2</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"134\">4</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"34\">6</text></g>\n<text x=\"270\" y=\"374\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:13px\">Maths score x₁</text>\n<text x=\"28\" y=\"180\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 28 180)\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:13px\">Physics score x₂</text>\n<line x1=\"120\" y1=\"330\" x2=\"416\" y2=\"34\" style=\"stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:2.5\" marker-end=\"url(#f57a)\"/>\n<line x1=\"370\" y1=\"280\" x2=\"174\" y2=\"84\" style=\"stroke:var(--live);stroke-width:2\" marker-end=\"url(#f57b)\"/>\n<text x=\"390\" y=\"46\" text-anchor=\"end\" style=\"font-size:13px;fill:var(--accent);font-weight:700\">PC1 · 90%</text>\n<text x=\"164\" y=\"76\" text-anchor=\"end\" style=\"font-size:13px;fill:var(--live);font-weight:700\">PC2 · 10%</text>\n<g style=\"stroke:var(--muted);stroke-width:1.5;stroke-dasharray:3 3\"><line x1=\"220\" y1=\"180\" x2=\"245\" y2=\"205\"/><line x1=\"270\" y1=\"230\" x2=\"245\" y2=\"205\"/><line x1=\"320\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"295\" y2=\"105\"/><line x1=\"370\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"295\" y2=\"105\"/></g>\n<g style=\"fill:var(--accent)\"><rect x=\"241\" y=\"201\" width=\"8\" height=\"8\"/><rect x=\"291\" y=\"101\" width=\"8\" height=\"8\"/></g>\n<g style=\"fill:var(--panel);stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2\"><circle cx=\"170\" cy=\"280\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"220\" cy=\"180\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"270\" cy=\"230\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"320\" cy=\"80\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"370\" cy=\"130\" r=\"6\"/></g>\n<circle cx=\"270\" cy=\"180\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--next)\"/>\n<text x=\"300\" y=\"186\" style=\"font-size:13px;fill:var(--next);font-weight:600\">mean (4, 3)</text>\n<text x=\"615\" y=\"60\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:14px;font-weight:600\">Variance explained</text>\n<path d=\"M540 300 H700\" style=\"stroke:var(--line2);stroke-width:1.5\"/>\n<rect x=\"560\" y=\"120\" width=\"50\" height=\"180\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\"/>\n<rect x=\"630\" y=\"280\" width=\"50\" height=\"20\" style=\"fill:var(--live)\"/>\n<g text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:13px\">\n<text x=\"585\" y=\"110\">λ₁ = 4.5 (90%)</text><text x=\"655\" y=\"270\">λ₂ = 0.5 (10%)</text><text x=\"585\" y=\"320\">PC1</text><text x=\"655\" y=\"320\">PC2</text>\n</g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>Figure 5.7.1</b> PCA on the worked example's five students. PC1 (blue) runs along the diagonal, the direction of greatest spread; PC2 (orange) is perpendicular to it. Dotted lines drop each point onto PC1, and the squares mark the projections, which become the one-number scores. The bars show the eigenvalues: keeping PC1 alone keeps 90% of the variance.</figcaption>\n</figure>",
 "8": "<figure class=\"fig\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 384\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"ROC curve of the ten scored cases: a staircase from 0,0 to 1,1 with area 0.80 shaded, the random-guess diagonal, and the threshold 0.5 point at FPR 0.4, TPR 0.8; the sorted scores are listed on the right\">\n<polygon points=\"90,330 90,270 90,210 150,210 150,150 150,90 210,90 270,90 270,30 330,30 390,30 390,330\" style=\"fill:var(--accent-soft)\"/>\n<path d=\"M90 330 H396 M90 330 V24 M150 330 v5 M210 330 v5 M270 330 v5 M330 330 v5 M390 330 v5 M90 270 h-5 M90 210 h-5 M90 150 h-5 M90 90 h-5 M90 30 h-5\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:var(--line2);stroke-width:1.5\"/>\n<g fill=\"currentColor\" text-anchor=\"middle\" style=\"font-size:13px\"><text x=\"90\" y=\"350\">0</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"350\">0.2</text><text x=\"210\" y=\"350\">0.4</text><text x=\"270\" y=\"350\">0.6</text><text x=\"330\" y=\"350\">0.8</text><text x=\"390\" y=\"350\">1</text></g>\n<g fill=\"currentColor\" text-anchor=\"end\" style=\"font-size:13px\"><text x=\"80\" y=\"334\">0</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"274\">0.2</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"214\">0.4</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"154\">0.6</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"94\">0.8</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"34\">1</text></g>\n<text x=\"240\" y=\"374\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:13px\">False positive rate (FPR)</text>\n<text x=\"30\" y=\"180\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 30 180)\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:13px\">True positive rate (recall)</text>\n<line x1=\"90\" y1=\"330\" x2=\"390\" y2=\"30\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);stroke-width:1.5;stroke-dasharray:6 4\"/>\n<text x=\"186\" y=\"252\" style=\"font-size:13px;fill:var(--muted)\">random: AUC = 0.5</text>\n<polyline points=\"90,330 90,270 90,210 150,210 150,150 150,90 210,90 270,90 270,30 330,30 390,30\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:3\"/>\n<text x=\"330\" y=\"200\" text-anchor=\"middle\" style=\"font-size:15px;fill:var(--accent);font-weight:700\">AUC = 0.80</text>\n<circle cx=\"210\" cy=\"90\" r=\"7\" style=\"fill:var(--live)\"/>\n<text x=\"258\" y=\"74\" text-anchor=\"end\" style=\"font-size:13px;fill:var(--live);font-weight:600\">at 0.5: (0.4, 0.8)</text>\n<text x=\"585\" y=\"40\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:14px;font-weight:600\">Cases, highest score first</text>\n<g fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:13px;font-family:var(--mono)\">\n<text x=\"520\" y=\"70\">0.95  P  ↑</text><text x=\"520\" y=\"96\">0.85  P  ↑</text><text x=\"520\" y=\"122\">0.80  N  →</text><text x=\"520\" y=\"148\">0.70  P  ↑</text><text x=\"520\" y=\"174\">0.60  P  ↑</text><text x=\"520\" y=\"200\">0.55  N  →</text><text x=\"520\" y=\"226\">0.45  N  →</text><text x=\"520\" y=\"252\">0.40  P  ↑</text><text x=\"520\" y=\"278\">0.30  N  →</text><text x=\"520\" y=\"304\">0.20  N  →</text>\n</g>\n<line x1=\"500\" y1=\"212\" x2=\"680\" y2=\"212\" style=\"stroke:var(--live);stroke-width:1.5;stroke-dasharray:5 3\"/>\n<text x=\"680\" y=\"334\" text-anchor=\"end\" style=\"font-size:13px;fill:var(--muted)\">↑ up 0.2 · → right 0.2</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>Figure 5.8.1</b> The ROC curve of the worked example. Each positive in the sorted list (right) moves the curve up and each negative moves it right; the orange dashed line in the list is the 0.5 threshold, which gives the orange point. The shaded area is the AUC, 0.80. A perfect model would go straight up to the corner (0, 1); this one hugs the left edge at first because its most confident cases are mostly right.</figcaption>\n</figure>",
 "9": "<figure class=\"fig\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 380\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Line chart of monthly UPI payments from January to August rising from 120 to 170 thousand, with the 3-month moving-average forecast and the exponential-smoothing forecast both running below the actual values, and September forecasts of 159.3 and 153.1\">\n<path d=\"M70 320 H620 M70 320 V36 M70 280 h-5 M70 200 h-5 M70 120 h-5 M70 40 h-5\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:var(--line2);stroke-width:1.5\"/>\n<path d=\"M70 280 H620 M70 200 H620 M70 120 H620\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:var(--line);stroke-width:1\"/>\n<g fill=\"currentColor\" text-anchor=\"end\" style=\"font-size:13px\"><text x=\"60\" y=\"284\">120</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"204\">140</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"124\">160</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"44\">180</text></g>\n<g fill=\"currentColor\" text-anchor=\"middle\" style=\"font-size:13px\"><text x=\"80\" y=\"340\">Jan</text><text x=\"145\" y=\"340\">Feb</text><text x=\"210\" y=\"340\">Mar</text><text x=\"275\" y=\"340\">Apr</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"340\">May</text><text x=\"405\" y=\"340\">Jun</text><text x=\"470\" y=\"340\">Jul</text><text x=\"535\" y=\"340\">Aug</text><text x=\"600\" y=\"340\">Sep</text></g>\n<text x=\"340\" y=\"368\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:13px\">Month</text>\n<text x=\"24\" y=\"180\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 24 180)\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:13px\">UPI payments (thousand)</text>\n<line x1=\"567\" y1=\"320\" x2=\"567\" y2=\"60\" style=\"stroke:var(--line2);stroke-width:1.5;stroke-dasharray:4 4\"/>\n<text x=\"600\" y=\"56\" text-anchor=\"middle\" style=\"font-size:13px;fill:var(--muted)\">forecast</text>\n<polyline points=\"80,280 145,232 210,248 275,200 340,152 405,168 470,120 535,80\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:3\"/>\n<g style=\"fill:var(--accent)\"><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"280\" r=\"5\"/><circle cx=\"145\" cy=\"232\" r=\"5\"/><circle cx=\"210\" cy=\"248\" r=\"5\"/><circle cx=\"275\" cy=\"200\" r=\"5\"/><circle cx=\"340\" cy=\"152\" r=\"5\"/><circle cx=\"405\" cy=\"168\" r=\"5\"/><circle cx=\"470\" cy=\"120\" r=\"5\"/><circle cx=\"535\" cy=\"80\" r=\"5\"/></g>\n<polyline points=\"275,253.3 340,226.7 405,200 470,173.3 535,146.7 600,122.7\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:var(--next);stroke-width:2.5;stroke-dasharray:8 5\"/>\n<polyline points=\"145,280 210,265.6 275,260.3 340,242.2 405,215.2 470,201 535,176.7 600,147.7\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:var(--live);stroke-width:2.5;stroke-dasharray:2 4\"/>\n<circle cx=\"600\" cy=\"122.7\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--next)\"/><circle cx=\"600\" cy=\"147.7\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--live)\"/>\n<text x=\"610\" y=\"127\" style=\"font-size:13px;fill:var(--next);font-weight:700\">MA 159.3</text>\n<text x=\"610\" y=\"152\" style=\"font-size:13px;fill:var(--live);font-weight:700\">SES 153.1</text>\n<line x1=\"90\" y1=\"56\" x2=\"120\" y2=\"56\" style=\"stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:3\"/><text x=\"128\" y=\"61\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:13px\">actual payments</text>\n<line x1=\"90\" y1=\"78\" x2=\"120\" y2=\"78\" style=\"stroke:var(--next);stroke-width:2.5;stroke-dasharray:8 5\"/><text x=\"128\" y=\"83\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:13px\">3-month moving-average forecast</text>\n<line x1=\"90\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"120\" y2=\"100\" style=\"stroke:var(--live);stroke-width:2.5;stroke-dasharray:2 4\"/><text x=\"128\" y=\"105\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size:13px\">exponential smoothing, α = 0.3</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>Figure 5.9.1</b> Monthly UPI payments to a college canteen with the two forecasts of the worked example. Each forecast point is made one month ahead from earlier values only. Notice that both forecast lines run below the actual series all the way: a rising trend leaves simple averages behind, and smoothing with α = 0.3 lags even more than the 3-month average.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
}